<title>USA: U.S. chain store sales up 1.7 pct - BTM/Schroders.</title>
<headline>U.S. chain store sales up 1.7 pct - BTM/Schroders.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-02-19</dateline>
<text>
<p>U.S. chain store sales rose 1.7 percent in the week ended February 15 from the prior week, according to the seasonally adjusted BTM/Schroders weekly chain store sales index.</p>
<p>Sales for the week were up 5.1 percent on a year-over-year basis, while the month-to-date index was up 1.8 percent from the prior month.</p>
<p>&quot;Sales were generally on-to-above plan for most retailers,&quot; the report said. &quot;Some retailers noted that the shift in Valentine's Day later in the week compared to last year boosted year-ago comparisons late in the week,&quot; it said.</p>
<p>((--N.A. Treasury Desk, 212-859-1660))</p>
